        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Closing tags without whitespace no longer end comment/verbatim blocks",
        "explanation": "The unnamed closing regexes require at least one non-newline whitespace character after `{%`. The old lexer compared the stripped content, so `{%endverbatim%}` and `{%endcomment%}` closed their blocks. Now, after `{% verbatim %}` or `{% comment %}`, the raw splitter never matches `{%endverbatim%}`. The rest of the template becomes one text token and the parser raises an unclosed-tag error. This breaks templates that used to work. The named-verbatim regex uses `*`, so it is inconsistent with these two.",
        "suggestion": "Use `[^\\S\\n]*` instead of `[^\\S\\n]+` in `_comment_end_re` and `_verbatim_end_re`. The opening tag still needs a word boundary after the tag name.",
        "evidence": "r\"%s[^\\S\\n]+endverbatim[^\\S\\n]*%s\"",
        "confidence": 0.5,
        "id": "bb12358907e8",
